CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kmalloc(sizeof(*map)...) over kmalloc(sizeof(struct pci2phy_map)...)
#171: FILE: arch/x86/kernel/cpu/perf_event_intel_uncore_snb.c:424:
+		map = kmalloc(sizeof(struct pci2phy_map), GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

